<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Organisation of African Unity</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Organisation of African Unity was an intergovernmental body of independent African states founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> in 1963. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> played a leading role in its creation. Its establishment confirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>'s role as a diplomatic centre of African independence, an important legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, and it was replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a> in 2002.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/organisation-of-african-unity.jpg" alt="Organisation of African Unity" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Organization of African Unity · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Organization_of_African_Unity_(1970%E2%80%932002);_Flag_of_the_African_Union_(2004%E2%80%932010).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
